0e47c0e7 (2822 1793923762009 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f429") (src . "test: row baseline line counts taken from the runner's merged output\n\nThe third column of rows-baseline.txt is wc -l of the runner's\n<name>.out, which launch.pl writes with the fixture's standard error\nmerged into its standard output. Ten entries had a count that this\nmachine's runner does not read; they are renewed, names, rows and\ndigests unchanged. RUN.md gains a paragraph saying how the column is\ncounted and which counts move while the fixture stays the same. The\ntable itself takes no comment: the check reads every line as an entry.\n\nWhere each count came from, read through launch.pl at the commit that\nwrote it and at this one:\n\n- change-stream-client, drafts-tools, import-symbols, ownership,\n  query-kinds and query-strata gain one line each, the machine-home\n  announcement a fixture's own THEOURGIA_HOME makes on standard error;\n  their counts had been taken with standard error apart.\n- datum-self gains 24 lines, one per own source added since its count\n  was taken with 53 sources listed; 77 are listed now.\n- liveness loses three lines. Two are the LV-6 lines it printed while\n  change-stream-guard-expect.sexp listed outline, which that file no\n  longer does; the third is unattributed (its own commit reads 47\n  against the recorded 48).\n- log15 gains two and runner-self seven lines, NOTE lines for signals\n  not sent because the process had already gone. log15 read 53 in\n  every run here; runner-self reads 114 or 115 with the timing, and\n  the gate's 114 is recorded.\n\nA differing line count still prints and does not refuse; the digest\nand the row count are the columns that refuse.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 642))))
