1ccac0c7 (2833 1793948035412 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f430") (src . "test: liveness LV-14 sized by a count, its receive a dead-actor guard\n\nThe LV-14 row sized its export from the flush calibration (files-for\n8000) and waited a fixed 40 s for the answer. An exported file costs\nmostly CPU, and more as the export grows: about 11 ms a file at 843\nfiles, 15 at 3100 and 19 at 5000, on a machine whose calibration reads\n10 ms. Where flushes are cheap the calibration sized the export at 2200\nto 5500 files; past about 3100 the export outlasted the 40 s receive and\nthe row's third line read FAIL although the export answered ok, and past\nabout 5000 the log wait after it failed too. The row's other clock is\nthe kill: a command line, which under load here took 5.2 s to return,\nafter a 508-file export had already answered.\n\nThe row now exports 1500 files. The main thread's receive is capped at\n180 s as a guard against a dead actor; the actor's own 30 s without a\nbyte, reset by every keepalive, stays the progress clock. One\ndiagnostics line is printed always (n, the kill's time, the answer's\ntime after the kill returned, what arrived), and the third want shows\nwhat arrived when it fails. The liveness entry of rows-baseline.txt is\nrenewed: 41 rows, 46 lines (the new line), the new digest.\n\nRead here: 10 runs alone, ok ok ok each, the answer 16.3 to 18.1 s after\na kill of 0.21 s; 3 runs with another fixture looping beside it, ok ok\nok, 16.9 to 18.6 s; n forced to 3100 and 5000 on a copy, ok ok ok, the\nanswer after 42.2 s and 90.7 s. Every other row reads as before. The\nfixture takes 8 to 11 s longer.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 643))))
